# Waivers for pre-existing findings carried across releases.
# Grouped by file. Each entry: file_glob | pattern | reason

# --- config_flow.py ---

# Coordinator fetches account-wide data; single-box users unaffected
custom_components/firewalla/config_flow.py | box_gid | single-box deployment

# --- coordinator.py ---

# Firewalla API returns integer delta-seconds, not HTTP-date
custom_components/firewalla/coordinator.py | Retry-After | Firewalla API uses integer delta-seconds only

# 429 sleep inside response context: bounded by API_TIMEOUT (30s)
custom_components/firewalla/coordinator.py | sleep | bounded by API_TIMEOUT

# WAN data may lag by one sample interval; sensors expose sample_seconds
custom_components/firewalla/coordinator.py | stale | known limitation, documented

# Single-box MSP tokens include flow endpoint access
custom_components/firewalla/coordinator.py | 403 | MSP tokens include flow endpoint access

# 25 Mbps trigger is appropriate for multi-gigabit links
custom_components/firewalla/coordinator.py | 25 Mbps | appropriate for multi-gigabit capacity experiment

# Non-overlapping sample windows make watermark advancement safe
custom_components/firewalla/coordinator.py | watermark | non-overlapping windows

# box_gid comes from validated config entry, not user input
custom_components/firewalla/coordinator.py | box_gid | from validated config entry

# process_flows bucketing loop: bounded by WAN_PEAK_RETENTION_SECONDS clamp
# and WAN_PEAK_MAX_PAGES pagination limit
custom_components/firewalla/coordinator.py | process_flows | bounded by retention window and pagination limits
custom_components/firewalla/coordinator.py | block or significantly delay | bounded pagination

# Query filter and constant are both 1MB; constant only affects sensor display
custom_components/firewalla/coordinator.py | total:>1MB | constant and query are both 1MB

